From: BTCM SW Team <btcm-sw-team@squareup.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Force verification regardless of OTP state

Treat the board as locked for verification policy, regardless of the lock
OTP or user unlock register. The existing late-init path restores verify=y
before boot scripts run, including when the saved environment has verify=n.

Apply only with UBOOT_FORCE_VERIFY = "1". This is a build-time override,
not an environment switch, and does not write OTP or establish hardware
secure boot. Signed boot artifacts matching the configured keys are still
required; release boot scripts also require a valid AVB rootfs.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Proto board verification policy]
---
 board/st/stm32mp1/stm32mp1.c | 24 ++----------------------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

diff --git a/board/st/stm32mp1/stm32mp1.c b/board/st/stm32mp1/stm32mp1.c
--- a/board/st/stm32mp1/stm32mp1.c
+++ b/board/st/stm32mp1/stm32mp1.c
@@ -818,28 +818,8 @@ static int proto_cb_get_part_info(struct blk_desc *mmc_dev, const char *name, struct disk_partition *info)
 	return -ENOENT;
 }
 static bool proto_cb_device_locked(void){
-	uint32_t lock_reg = 0;
-	int ret = fuse_read(PROTO_CB_FUSE_BANK, PROTO_CB_DEVICE_LOCK_OTP_INDEX, &lock_reg);
-	if (ret) {
-		log_err("Failed to read device lock reg!");
-		return true;
-	}
-
-	// If lock OTP is not set, device is not locked
-	if ((lock_reg & PROTO_CB_DEVICE_LOCK_OTP_MASK) == 0) {
-		return false;
-	}
-
-	// Lock OTP is set, check if user has unlocked
-	uint32_t unlock_reg = 0;
-	ret = fuse_read(PROTO_CB_FUSE_BANK, PROTO_CB_FUSE_UNLOCK_REG_WORD_IDX, &unlock_reg);
-	if (ret) {
-		log_err("Failed to read device unlock reg!");
-		return true;
-	}
-
-	// Device is locked if unlock register is not set
-	return unlock_reg == 0;
+	/* Build-time policy override; do not consult or modify OTP. */
+	return true;
 }
 
 static void proto_cb_set_hostname(void){
